a book, teach a paid class from them. Say where they came from.


A NOTE ON WHAT IS AND IS NOT HERE

This repository holds content. The Paathshaala player that reads it, the
website that lists it and the editor that writes it are separate and are not
open source. That asymmetry is deliberate: the part that must stay reusable
forever is the part that teaches.

Each pack also declares its own licence in its manifest.json. Where a pack
declares something other than CC-BY-4.0, that declaration governs that pack.

Third-party material inside a pack carries its own licence, recorded beside
the pack and credited on the screen it appears on.
